# Introduction to integrating Tailwind CSS

React Material provides seamless integration with Tailwind CSS, allowing you to use Material Design 3 tokens and utilities alongside Tailwind's utility classes.

## Installation

First, make sure you have both React Material and Tailwind CSS installed:

```bash
npm install react-material tailwindcss
```

## Setup

### 1. Import Tailwind CSS

In your main CSS file (typically `globals.css` or `index.css`), import Tailwind CSS:

```css
@import "tailwindcss";
```

### 2. Add Material Design Theme Configuration

Add the Material Design theme configuration using the `@theme` directive. This makes Material Design 3 tokens available as CSS custom properties:

```css
@theme {
  /* Material Design 3 Color Tokens */
  --color-*: initial;
  --color-background: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-background));
  --color-on-background: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-background));
  --color-surface: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-surface));
  --color-surface-dim: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-surface-dim));
  --color-surface-bright: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-surface-bright));
  --color-surface-container-lowest: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-surface-container-lowest));
  --color-surface-container-low: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-surface-container-low));
  --color-surface-container: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-surface-container));
  --color-surface-container-high: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-surface-container-high));
  --color-surface-container-highest: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-surface-container-highest));
  --color-on-surface: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-surface));
  --color-on-surface-variant: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-surface-variant));
  --color-outline: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-outline));
  --color-outline-variant: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-outline-variant));
  --color-inverse-surface: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-inverse-surface));
  --color-inverse-on-surface: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-inverse-on-surface));
  --color-primary: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-primary));
  --color-primary-dim: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-primary-dim));
  --color-on-primary: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-primary));
  --color-primary-container: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-primary-container));
  --color-on-primary-container: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-primary-container));
  --color-primary-fixed: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-primary-fixed));
  --color-primary-fixed-dim: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-primary-fixed-dim));
  --color-on-primary-fixed: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-primary-fixed));
  --color-on-primary-fixed-variant: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-primary-fixed-variant));
  --color-inverse-primary: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-inverse-primary));
  --color-secondary: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-secondary));
  --color-secondary-dim: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-secondary-dim));
  --color-on-secondary: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-secondary));
  --color-secondary-container: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-secondary-container));
  --color-on-secondary-container: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-secondary-container));
  --color-secondary-fixed: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-secondary-fixed));
  --color-secondary-fixed-dim: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-secondary-fixed-dim));
  --color-on-secondary-fixed: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-secondary-fixed));
  --color-on-secondary-fixed-variant: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-secondary-fixed-variant));
  --color-tertiary: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-tertiary));
  --color-tertiary-dim: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-tertiary-dim));
  --color-on-tertiary: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-tertiary));
  --color-tertiary-container: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-tertiary-container));
  --color-on-tertiary-container: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-tertiary-container));
  --color-tertiary-fixed: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-tertiary-fixed));
  --color-tertiary-fixed-dim: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-tertiary-fixed-dim));
  --color-on-tertiary-fixed: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-tertiary-fixed));
  --color-on-tertiary-fixed-variant: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-tertiary-fixed-variant));
  --color-error: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-error));
  --color-error-dim: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-error-dim));
  --color-on-error: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-error));
  --color-error-container: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-error-container));
  --color-on-error-container: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-error-container));
  --color-on-on-primary: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-on-primary));

  /* Material Design 3 Radius Tokens */
  --radius-none: 0rem;
  --radius-xs: var(--m3-util-rounding-extra-small);
  --radius-sm: var(--m3-util-rounding-small);
  --radius-md: var(--m3-util-rounding-medium);
  --radius-lg: var(--m3-util-rounding-large);
  --radius-xl: var(--m3-util-rounding-extra-large);
  --radius-2xl: var(--m3-util-rounding-extra-extra-large);
  --radius-full: var(--m3-util-rounding-full);

  /* Material Design 3 Motion Tokens */
  --default-transition-timing-function: var(--ease-normal);
  --ease-*: initial;
  --ease-fast-spatial: var(--m3-util-easing-fast-spatial);
  --ease-spatial: var(--m3-util-easing-spatial);
  --ease-slow-spatial: var(--m3-util-easing-slow-spatial);
  --ease-fast: var(--m3-util-easing-fast);
  --ease-normal: var(--m3-util-easing);
  --ease-slow: var(--m3-util-easing-slow);
  --ease-curve: var(--m3-util-curve);
  --ease-curve-decel: var(--m3-util-curve-decel);
  --ease-curve-accel: var(--m3-util-curve-accel);
}
```

### 3. Import Material Design Utilities

After setting up the theme configuration, import the React Material Tailwind utilities in your root React app file (e.g., `App.tsx`, `main.tsx`, or `index.tsx`):

```tsx
import "react-material/tailwind.css";
```

> Due to Tailwind CSS's compilation process, the `@theme` directive alone is not sufficient for dynamic theming. The `react-material/tailwind.css` file contains pre-compiled utility classes that map to the Material Design 3 color tokens, enabling per-content theming support. This ensures that components can dynamically respond to theme changes at runtime.

## Complete Example

Here's a complete example of your setup:

### CSS File (globals.css)

```css
@import "tailwindcss";

@theme {
  --default-font-family: roboto, sans-serif;
  --font-roboto: roboto, sans-serif;
  --font-dmsans: dmsans, sans-serif;

  --color-*: initial;
  --color-background: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-background));
  --color-on-background: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-background));
  --color-surface: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-surface));
  /* ... other color tokens ... */

  --radius-none: 0rem;
  --radius-xs: var(--m3-util-rounding-extra-small);
  /* ... other radius tokens ... */

  --ease-fast: var(--m3-util-easing-fast);
  /* ... other easing tokens ... */
}

@layer base {
  :root {
    --m3-font: var(--font-roboto), system-ui, sans-serif;
    --m3-font-display: var(--font-dmsans), system-ui, sans-serif;
    --m3-font-headline: var(--font-dmsans), system-ui, sans-serif;
    --m3-font-title: var(--font-dmsans), system-ui, sans-serif;
    --m3-font-label: var(--font-roboto), system-ui, sans-serif;
    --m3-font-body: var(--font-roboto), system-ui, sans-serif;
  }
  
  body {
    @apply bg-surface text-on-surface;
  }
}
```

### Root React App File (App.tsx)

```tsx
;
import "./globals.css"; // Your main CSS file with theme configuration
import "react-material/tailwind.css"; // Import Material Design utilities

function App() {
  return (
    <div className="min-h-screen bg-background">
      {/* Your app content */}
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
```

## Using Material Design Utilities

Once configured, you can use Material Design utilities alongside regular Tailwind classes:

```jsx
export function Example() {
  return (
    <div className="bg-surface-container p-4 rounded-md">
      <h1 className="text-on-surface text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
        Material Design Card
      </h1>
      <p className="text-on-surface-variant mb-4">
        This card uses Material Design 3 color tokens.
      </p>
      <button className="bg-primary text-on-primary px-4 py-2 rounded-full hover:bg-primary-dim transition-colors">
        Primary Button
      </button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Why Both `@theme` and `tailwind.css` Are Required

Tailwind CSS has a fundamental limitation when it comes to dynamic theming:

### The Problem
- Tailwind CSS compiles utility classes at **build time**
- The `@theme` directive defines CSS custom properties, but Tailwind cannot generate utility classes that reference these properties dynamically
- Traditional Tailwind utilities like `bg-red-500` are static and compiled to fixed color values

### The Solution
React Material solves this by providing:

1. **`@theme` directive**: Defines all Material Design 3 tokens as CSS custom properties
2. **`react-material/tailwind.css`**: Contains pre-compiled utility classes that reference the custom properties

```css
/* Example of what's in react-material/tailwind.css */
.bg-primary {
  background-color: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-primary));
}

.text-on-primary {
  color: rgb(var(--m3-scheme-on-primary));
}
```

This approach enables:
- ✅ **Dynamic theming**: Colors change when CSS custom properties update
- ✅ **Runtime theme switching**: No rebuild required for theme changes
- ✅ **Per-content theming**: Different parts of your app can have different themes
- ✅ **Dark mode support**: Automatic adaptation to theme changes

